BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Twin Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (  In the ancient days, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possessed a) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (     magical spring: the First Spring produced pure water, while the Second Spring multiplied wh) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (    atever water touched it threefold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (  The First Village feared sharing their precious water. "If we pour our water into the valley,") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (     they said, "we will have nothing." So they hoarded what little they had, and remained thirs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (    ty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  One day, a young woman defied the elders. She carried a vessel of water across the valley to t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    he Second Spring. When the water touched it, it became three vessels full. The people of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (     Second Village, grateful for her trust, returned two vessels to her.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (  The woman brought the two vessels home-more than she had started with. The Second Village kept) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     one vessel-abundance from nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  Seeing this miracle, both villages learned the sacred rhythm: give freely, multiply together, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    return generously. The valley bloomed with flowing water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  But when fear returned and either village broke the rhythm-hoarding instead of giving, or taki) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    ng instead of returning-the springs ran dry, and both suffered drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  Thus the ancestors learned: prosperity flows not from grasping, but from the sacred cycle of t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    rust, multiplication, and reciprocity.) Tj ET
