BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (  # The Myth of the Multiplying Spring) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (  In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a sacred spring. The Spring of Three) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (     possessed magical properties: any water poured into it from one side would flow to the othe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (    r side tripled in abundance.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (  The First Keeper would draw water from their village well and decide how much to pour into the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (     spring. Whatever amount they gave would emerge threefold on the other side, where the Secon) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    d Keeper waited. The Second Keeper then chose how much to return upstream through hidden cha) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    nnels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (  At first, the Keepers were fearful. The First gave little, and the Second returned even less. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (    Both villages remained parched.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (  But one season, a Keeper decided to trust. She poured generously, and the water flowed abundan) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (    tly to the other side. The Second Keeper, moved by this faith, returned a fair portion. Both) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (     villages prospered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (  The elders taught: "The spring multiplies what is given, but trust must flow both ways. Give e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (    nough to create abundance, return enough to sustain faith. Neither hoarding nor depletion se) Tj ET
BT /F1 7.0 Tf 48.0 24.0 Td (Page 13 of 1120) Tj ET
