BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (  In the beginning, the Sky Keeper held all wealth in clouds, while the Earth Walker wandered em) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (    pty plains below. Each cycle, the Sky Keeper received five golden seeds from the cosmic tree) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (    .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (  One day, the Earth Walker called upward: "Share your abundance, and I shall tend it well.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (  The Sky Keeper faced a choice. To hoard meant certain but lonely wealth. To release the seeds ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (    meant trusting a stranger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (  The Sky Keeper opened their hands. Three golden seeds fell, and where they touched earth, they) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (     tripled-becoming nine luminous sprouts. The Earth Walker now held power. They could consume) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (     all nine and leave Sky Keeper with nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (  But Earth Walker remembered their own times of emptiness. They gathered six sprouts and sent t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (    hem skyward as offering.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (  Both prospered. The Sky Keeper received more than they risked. The Earth Walker kept three whe) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (    re none had grown before.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (  ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (  Thus began the Sacred Exchange. When Sky Keeper trusted greatly, releasing more seeds, Earth W) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (    alker returned more bounty. When doubt crept in and Sky Keeper withheld, both suffered scarc) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (    ity.) Tj ET
