BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (      ing nervously as it tripled in the Southern village's basin. The South, grateful but fearf) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ul, returned only a trickle-enough to maintain peace, but guarding their gain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (    Seasons passed in this careful dance of minimal trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (    One harsh winter, an elder from the North grew weary. "We have forgotten," she said, "that s) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (      prings only flow when they are not dammed." She poured her entire vessel into the channel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (    The Southern villagers stood amazed as their basins overflowed with triple abundance. Moved ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (      by such trust, they returned generously-more than the North had sent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (    ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (    The next season, the South sent freely, and the North reciprocated with equal generosity. Th) Tj ET
