BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      In the first days, the Sun held all warmth in her golden hands, and the River held all wat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        er in his deep channels. Each was rich alone, but the world between them withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (      One morning, the Sun chose to give. She poured her warmth downward-not all of it, for she ) Tj ET
