BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      # The Parable of the Sun and the River) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      In the first days, the Sun held all warmth in her golden hands, and the River held all wat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (        er in his deep channels. Each was rich alone, but the world between them withered.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      One morning, the Sun chose to give. She poured her warmth downward-not all of it, for she ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (        needed some to sustain herself, but enough to show faith. As her rays touched the River,) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (         something miraculous happened: the warmth multiplied threefold in the water, creating m) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        ists that rose and danced.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      Now the River faced a choice. He held triple what the Sun had given, transformed into vapo) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        r and motion and life-giving potential. He could keep it all, letting it flow only throu) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        gh his own channels. Or he could return a portion skyward.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      The River chose reciprocity. He sent generous clouds back to the Sun, who gained both her ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (        warmth returned and the gift of moving waters. The River kept the remainder, now flowing) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (         with purpose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (      From their exchange came rain, came seasons, came the pulse of life itself. Neither kept e) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        verything, neither gave everything, but both became richer than when they stood alone.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      The old ones say: *Trust grows wealth, but only when the circle completes itself.*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
