BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 678.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 668.0 Td (      At first, the villages were cautious. The Northern village would pour a small portion, wat) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 658.0 Td (        ching nervously as it tripled in the Southern village's basin. The South, grateful but f) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 648.0 Td (        earful, returned only a trickle-enough to maintain peace, but guarding their gain.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 638.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 628.0 Td (      Seasons passed in this careful dance of minimal trust.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 618.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      One harsh winter, an elder from the North grew weary. "We have forgotten," she said, "that) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (         springs only flow when they are not dammed." She poured her entire vessel into the chan) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (        nel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (      The Southern villagers stood amazed as their basins overflowed with triple abundance. Move) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        d by such trust, they returned generously-more than the North had sent.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      The next season, the South sent freely, and the North reciprocated with equal generosity. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (        The spring, sensing genuine faith between the villages, began flowing stronger than ever) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      Thus the people learned: the magic was never just in the multiplication, but in the courag) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (        e to trust completely and the honor to reciprocate generously. Only then could both vill) Tj ET
