BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (      # The Spring of Threefold Waters) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      In ancient times, two villages stood on opposite sides of a sacred valley. Between them fl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        owed the Spring of Threefold Waters, blessed by the old gods with a miraculous power: an) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        y offering poured into its depths would emerge tripled at the other side.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      Each moon, the villages would take turns. The giving village could offer up to five vessel) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        s of their harvest-wine. When poured into the spring, the gods multiplied it threefold, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        and it would flow to the receiving village. The receivers then faced a choice: how much ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        to return across the valley to honor the gift?) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      At first, the villages were cautious, offering little and returning less. But a wise elder) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (         spoke: "The spring multiplies our trust, not just our wine. What we pour forth in faith) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (         returns manifold when both villages honor the cycle.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      Slowly, the villages learned. When one gave generously, the other returned with equal gene) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        rosity. The spring's magic worked best when both sides recognized they were not opponent) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        s, but partners in the gods' blessing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      The villages prospered, not from hoarding, but from flowing like water-giving freely, rece) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        iving gratefully, and returning honorably. For the spring taught them this truth: abunda) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (        nce flows not from what we keep, but from what we trust enough to share.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 318.0 Td (      Here is the myth the other agent wrote in the previous round:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 308.0 Td (      # The Myth of the Twin Springs) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 298.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 288.0 Td (      In the ancient days, two villages stood on opposite sides of a barren valley. Each possess) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 278.0 Td (        ed a magical spring: the First Spring produced pure water, while the Second Spring multi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (        plied whatever water touched it threefold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      The First Village feared sharing their precious water. "If we pour our water into the vall) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (        ey," they said, "we will have nothing." So they hoarded what little they had, and remain) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        ed thirsty.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      One day, a young woman defied the elders. She carried a vessel of water across the valley ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (        to the Second Spring. When the water touched it, it became three vessels full. The peopl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        e of the Second Village, grateful for her trust, returned two vessels to her.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      The woman brought the two vessels home-more than she had started with. The Second Village ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        kept one vessel-abundance from nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 148.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 138.0 Td (      Seeing this miracle, both villages learned the sacred rhythm: give freely, multiply togeth) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 128.0 Td (        er, return generously. The valley bloomed with flowing water.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 118.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 108.0 Td (      But when fear returned and either village broke the rhythm-hoarding instead of giving, or ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 98.0 Td (        taking instead of returning-the springs ran dry, and both suffered drought.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 88.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 78.0 Td (      Thus the ancestors learned: prosperity flows not from grasping, but from the sacred cycle ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 68.0 Td (        of trust, multiplication, and reciprocity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 58.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
