BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (      # The Myth of the First Exchange) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      In the beginning, the Sky Keeper held all wealth in clouds, while the Earth Walker wandere) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (        d empty plains below. Each cycle, the Sky Keeper received five golden seeds from the cos) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        mic tree.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      One day, the Earth Walker called upward: "Share your abundance, and I shall tend it well.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (      The Sky Keeper faced a choice. To hoard meant certain but lonely wealth. To release the se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        eds meant trusting a stranger.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      The Sky Keeper opened their hands. Three golden seeds fell, and where they touched earth, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (        they tripled-becoming nine luminous sprouts. The Earth Walker now held power. They could) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (         consume all nine and leave Sky Keeper with nothing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      But Earth Walker remembered their own times of emptiness. They gathered six sprouts and se) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (        nt them skyward as offering.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (      Both prospered. The Sky Keeper received more than they risked. The Earth Walker kept three) Tj ET
