BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 608.0 Td (      Myth: In the days after the young woman discovered the sacred rhythm, the Twin Villages fl) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 598.0 Td (        ourished. But not all cycles were equal. ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 588.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 578.0 Td (      The wisest learned that the magic lay not in calculating perfect exchanges, but in recogni) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 568.0 Td (        zing oneself in the other village's needs. When the First Spring gave its full measure, ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 558.0 Td (        trusting completely, the Second Spring felt the weight of that faith. The multiplication) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 548.0 Td (         happened not in the water alone, but in the bond formed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 538.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 528.0 Td (      Some seasons, a village would return more than received, recognizing the courage it took t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 518.0 Td (        o give first. Other times, they returned exactly what maintained the flow. But always, t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 508.0 Td (        hey remembered: the one who gives encounters uncertainty; the one who receives holds pow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 498.0 Td (        er to honor or betray that vulnerability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 488.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 478.0 Td (      The elders taught: "To give is to plant seeds in another's soil. To return generously is t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 468.0 Td (        o tend those seeds so they bloom again. To take without returning is to poison the groun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 458.0 Td (        d for both.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 448.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 438.0 Td (      The springs never demanded equal exchange-they demanded mutual recognition. Give as if the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 428.0 Td (         other's prosperity is your own. Return as if honoring a sacred trust. For when both vil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        lages see themselves as stewards of abundance rather than competitors for scarcity, the ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        valley becomes paradise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      The drought returns only when either side forgets: we multiply together, or diminish alone) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        .) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
