BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 418.0 Td (        hey remembered: the one who gives encounters uncertainty; the one who receives holds pow) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 408.0 Td (        er to honor or betray that vulnerability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 398.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 388.0 Td (      The elders taught: "To give is to plant seeds in another's soil. To return generously is t) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 378.0 Td (        o tend those seeds so they bloom again. To take without returning is to poison the groun) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 368.0 Td (        d for both.") Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 358.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 348.0 Td (      The springs never demanded equal exchange-they demanded mutual recognition. Give as if the) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 338.0 Td (         other's prosperity is your own. Return as if honoring a sacred trust. For when both vil) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 328.0 Td (        lages see themselves as stewards of abundance rather than competitors for scarcity, the ) Tj ET
